# Settings that belong to this machine, not to the repository.
#
# Copy this file to `server/.env` and fill in what you have. Git ignores that
# copy. Nothing here is required: every feed this service needs is free and
# asks for no key, and what is listed below only adds to that.
#
# The service reads this file itself on start, so it applies however you start
# it: `npm start`, `npm run dev`, or `npm run serve`.

# FantasyPros consensus rankings and ADP.
#
# Optional. Without it the board is built from Fantasy Football Calculator and
# Sleeper exactly as before. Get one at https://api.fantasypros.com/public/v2/docs
# — issued immediately, free, personal and non-commercial use.
#
# The free tier allows 50 requests a day and truncates its responses, so this
# service caches what it gets for hours at a time rather than asking again.
# Keep the key to yourself: it is yours personally and may not be shared or
# handed to anyone else.
FANTASYPROS_API_KEY=

# The season to read. Defaults to the current calendar year.
# DRAFT_YEAR=2026

# Where the service listens. Loopback only unless you change HOST, which you
# should not do on a network you do not trust: there is no authentication here.
# PORT=5178
# HOST=127.0.0.1
